														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1431095">
									

<p>Sorry, I had to downvote, because I'm just &#8230; not digging it.</p>
<p>There seem to be two concepts at work which are entirely separate from each other &#8230; the form that the SCP takes and the effect it has, with no obvious connection between the two. Frankly I found the idea of a guy with a light-bulb for a head and a lightswitch on his back a bit too comical, and the hallucinations that it causes a bit too vague to be scary. It causes hallucinations which make people hear ringing and drilling, which seem to drive people nuts. I think it needs more creep-factor when it comes to that.</p>
<p>I'd suggest re-writing it as a Safe rather than an Euclid, and playing up the more sinister creep rather than the &quot;it is dangerous and it can most definitely kill you&quot; stuff. That part feels a little forced. Good potential SCP though.</p>

							</div>

								
					
